{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20","id":1475034,"title":"Paths of Enlightenment in the Camarilla [V20]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-20T05:54:48-08:00","id":1475034,"title":"Paths of Enlightenment in the Camarilla [V20]","content":"So I was reading on the lore for V5 and I'm not a fan of about 90% of it (and not a fan of 99% of the new mechanics but that's besides the point), but I like the idea of the Lasombra joining the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> With so many Lasombra following Paths of Enlightenment (like the Prince of Milan, Giangaleazzo) would these Paths then disseminate among other Camarilla vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T06:58:51-08:00","id":1475039,"title":"","content":"Highly likely, also considering the spread of Blood Cults. <br /> <br /> Probably, many &quot;young&quot; Princes, which were educated into persecution against diverging moralities and Noddism, would still look at them with disdain, but others, like Elders and occultists, could be enthused. <br /> <br /> Honourable Accord could easily find asylum within the Camarilla, after being denounced as Forsaken by the Sabbat zealots. <br /> <br /> It should be one of the driving dynamics of political tension in nuCamarilla: of course, not every Path could be suitable for unlife in a Masquerade-abiding society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 02-20-2022, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T08:27:53-08:00","id":1475041,"title":"","content":"In V20? No. The Cam is Pro-humanity and, though some paths might slip under the radar (honourable accord) or reach some level of tacit acceptance (Settites are useful friends to have, Typhonists are fine so long as they keep it to themselves) The Cam must generally maintain the premise that Humanity is the chosen path because it's the best for the masquerade (and &quot;Maintaining the masquerade&quot; is a great premise for shafting neonates and rivals in a way that seems legaly justified). The Cam as an overall body doesn't have much sway over individual prices or cities so some exceptions may exist, but for the most part, it's convert or die, or at the very least shut up and don't spread that shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T09:30:37-08:00","id":1475045,"title":"","content":"Yes, you still need a V5esque setting, at least in direction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T10:56:55-08:00","id":1475048,"title":"","content":"Some older vamps may still be on Roads, of course. Though not openly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T11:17:49-08:00","id":1475049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475045#post1475045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you still need a V5esque setting, at least in direction</div> </div> </div> </div>Bruh, he's not talking V5. He doesn't like V5. We're not talking nuCam, we're talking Cam with a few more Lasombra. There's nothing about that requiring V5ification. <br /> <br /> <br /> V20 wise, there's always been a few Lasombra hiding among the cam, but if Sabbat Lasombra were to defect, they'd be under a lot of scrutiny and would need to live by the ideals of the Camarilla. IE they'd probably need to actually try harder than most to be humane. Relatively speaking the Lasombra are filled with very agressive and power hungry individuals, and their inclusion could destablize a city, so Ventrue and other lovers of the status quo are likely to find any reason to expel the Lasombra that they can, unless of course they've got a threat these new Lasombra can be pointed at. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla sees Gehenna cults as BadWrong. Secret cults? The Prince can be a member, but it can't be known that he's a member! The Lasombra are also drawn to religion (that whole dark void thing really puts the fear of god in them), they're suspect. <br /> <br /> Lasombra in the Cam are on thin ice. They'll thrive in a conflict, but smart vampires don't want conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T11:34:24-08:00","id":1475050,"title":"","content":"Whether it's controlling in order to preserve the Masquerade or it preserves the Masquerade to justify being controlling, I think we can say in good faith that the Cam in any edition of the game effectively has one set of laws for its small community of trusted ancient elders and another for the common riff-raff.<br /> <br /> In V20 in particular, the reader is told in multiple books that mention the topic that vampires on Paths are creepy, intense, and wrong-feeling even by vampire standards; even the ones whose Paths make them polite company for other vampires are going to draw attention when they're rubbing elbows with their food at the club. I'd see the Cam absolutely refusing to tolerate this in anyone who isn't an insider's insider. Like, Justicar or Justicar's favorite Archon, at bare minimum age and status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 02-20-2022, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T12:10:25-08:00","id":1475054,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is that the Cam's hard line anti-Path stance largely got written into the game before a lot of the more Cam friendly Paths were written. Revised and V20 both already have the idea that Paths are followed in the Cam on some level, even if not openly, or with extreme suspicion unless a well established Elder/etc.<br /> <br /> I don't think you need to go full V5 (as there was already a significant population of Lasobmra in the Cam as it was). Given there's already a few groups in the Cam that shouldn't struggle to find access to some Path, you just need a few of them to gain enough prestige in the Cam to push for some reforms around specific Paths; especially under the sale that it's better to put a vampire on a Path that's compatible with the Cam's ideals than lose them to other factions because strict Humanity isn't working for them. It's not hard to then turn Paths into part of the Cam power structure where young vampires seeking something other than Humanity just end up grinding away in service of a different set of Elders than those seeking other interests within the organization.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T13:29:32-08:00","id":1475058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475049#post1475049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bruh, he's not talking V5. He doesn't like V5. We're not talking nuCam, we're talking Cam with a few more Lasombra. There's nothing about that requiring V5ification. <br /> <br /> <br /> V20 wise, there's always been a few Lasombra hiding among the cam, but if Sabbat Lasombra were to defect, they'd be under a lot of scrutiny and would need to live by the ideals of the Camarilla. IE they'd probably need to actually try harder than most to be humane. Relatively speaking the Lasombra are filled with very agressive and power hungry individuals, and their inclusion could destablize a city, so Ventrue and other lovers of the status quo are likely to find any reason to expel the Lasombra that they can, unless of course they've got a threat these new Lasombra can be pointed at. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla sees Gehenna cults as BadWrong. Secret cults? The Prince can be a member, but it can't be known that he's a member! The Lasombra are also drawn to religion (that whole dark void thing really puts the fear of god in them), they're suspect. <br /> <br /> Lasombra in the Cam are on thin ice. They'll thrive in a conflict, but smart vampires don't want conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, V20 is more ruleset than setting, it's metaplot-agnostic.<br /> <br /> With just some Lasombra defecting (like, let's say, Kings and Queens of the Night) you are probably not going to get that many Path followers into the Cam to achieve pro-Paths reform. <br /> <br /> Camarilla's acceptance of Blood Cults in V5 is largely the result of the rise of Lilins and Church of Caine, along with mass hysteria and rise of Methuselah cults. All of these plot points are somewhat connected to the Sabbat weakening. <br /> <br /> In V20 default setting, with the Sabbat still going strong, Paths are too much associated with the Enemy and the Lasombra more likely to defect are those who probably will mostly be on Humanity (at lower levels perhaps). You also wouldn't probably get enough Path priests defecting, to make the conversion to Paths sustainable. <br /> <br /> You would probably see some secret acceptance among Elders for Power and Inner Voice and Honorable Accord, and greater numbers of Entelechy followers, but institutional incentives to Path tolerance are still low. <br /> <br /> You might get some more open acceptance of Paths, while still having the Sabbat big, if the Camarilla simultaneously accepts factions of the Lasombra, Setites, Assamites and maybe Ravnos. <br /> <br /> At that point, you might have enough traction, and diversity of Paths, to get them somewhat accepted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 02-20-2022, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T14:02:50-08:00","id":1475059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475049#post1475049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bruh, he's not talking V5. He doesn't like V5. We're not talking nuCam, we're talking Cam with a few more Lasombra. There's nothing about that requiring V5ification. <br /> <br /> <br /> V20 wise, there's always been a few Lasombra hiding among the cam, but if Sabbat Lasombra were to defect, they'd be under a lot of scrutiny and would need to live by the ideals of the Camarilla. IE they'd probably need to actually try harder than most to be humane. Relatively speaking the Lasombra are filled with very agressive and power hungry individuals, and their inclusion could destablize a city, so Ventrue and other lovers of the status quo are likely to find any reason to expel the Lasombra that they can, unless of course they've got a threat these new Lasombra can be pointed at. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla sees Gehenna cults as BadWrong. Secret cults? The Prince can be a member, but it can't be known that he's a member! The Lasombra are also drawn to religion (that whole dark void thing really puts the fear of god in them), they're suspect. <br /> <br /> Lasombra in the Cam are on thin ice. They'll thrive in a conflict, but smart vampires don't want conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its probably worth noting that defecting to the carmarilla is a level 1 sin for both path of night (repenting) and power and inner voice (giving up power) the two most common lasombra Sabbat Paths so its pretty likely most path lasombra stuck with the sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T00:20:44-08:00","id":1475086,"title":"","content":"Both in v5 and v20 paths of enlightenment are, mostly, corruptions of the old roads. In fact, paths were specifically made by the Sabbat in order to stave off the beast while rejecting their humanity.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla however reinforces humanity, primarily because it's easier to control humane neonates then those on a path. They'll claim it's about the masquerade, which is fair considering path followers can't Blush, but it's almost exclusively about control.<br /> <br /> So to answer the question, it's unlikely. The Camarilla will discourage it, and path following Lasombra will be very unlikely to share. Now that said, there could be a movement in the Anarchs, as the few non-Sabbat Tzimisce are defecting to their cause. Tzimisce, while just as unlikely to share, are more likely to given situational circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 02-21-2022, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T01:06:19-08:00","id":1475205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475059#post1475059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its probably worth noting that defecting to the carmarilla is a level 1 sin for both path of night (repenting) and power and inner voice (giving up power) the two most common lasombra Sabbat Paths so its pretty likely most path lasombra stuck with the sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes they weren't willing to suffer that small stain in order to survive, Lasombra are pragmatists rather than idealists in most cases. There are also ways of rationalising the decision to leave alongside switching to the Camarilla. Path of Night might leave the Sabbat in order to survive but not renounce their acts in the sect (at least if they're not well known) and then lie by omission. Path of Power &amp; the Inner Voice meanwhile could say that the Sabbat was rapidly losing power, it was spiralling and they'd ultimately lose what little power it had left. (Joining the Camarilla and seizing power in an international organisation is more effective.)<br /> <br /> Personally, I think a fair few elders will stick with their paths, they might in-turn teach them to their childer or loyal subordinates down the centuries. That's how paths will enter the Camarilla were I to wager, perhaps as part of one of the many new Blood Cults, perhaps on a personal basis. The Anarchs meanwhile are an open space for paths, the idea of Anarch communes springing up focussed on teaching and practising certain paths is very intriguing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T05:30:46-08:00","id":1475225,"title":"","content":"@Karos<br /> <br /> I agree with this. I think some Paths (Honorable Accord, Power and Inner Voice especially) would find quite the home in the Camarilla and could possibly create some secret societies around them, even if lip service is still paid to Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T05:32:14-08:00","id":1475226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475225#post1475225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Karos<br /> <br /> I agree with this. I think some Paths (Honorable Accord, Power and Inner Voice especially) would find quite the home in the Camarilla and could possibly create some secret societies around them, even if lip service is still paid to Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, small secret societies that make themselves useful to certain elders for protection, seem very fitting. You know a gentleman's club of Ventrue that follow Honourable Accord and are the Primogens biggest backers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T16:00:51-08:00","id":1475263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475205#post1475205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That assumes they weren't willing to suffer that small stain in order to survive, Lasombra are pragmatists rather than idealists in most cases. There are also ways of rationalising the decision to leave alongside switching to the Camarilla. Path of Night might leave the Sabbat in order to survive but not renounce their acts in the sect (at least if they're not well known) and then lie by omission. Path of Power &amp; the Inner Voice meanwhile could say that the Sabbat was rapidly losing power, it was spiralling and they'd ultimately lose what little power it had left. (Joining the Camarilla and seizing power in an international organisation is more effective.)<br /> <br /> Personally, I think a fair few elders will stick with their paths, they might in-turn teach them to their childer or loyal subordinates down the centuries. That's how paths will enter the Camarilla were I to wager, perhaps as part of one of the many new Blood Cults, perhaps on a personal basis. The Anarchs meanwhile are an open space for paths, the idea of Anarch communes springing up focussed on teaching and practising certain paths is very intriguing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A small stain is something of an understatement, a rank 1 sin is the emotional equivelant of feeding a child to its parents alive. With night I don't really think you could wrangle around repentance that way anymore than you can wrangle around any sin, you can't rationalise away murder as a humanity even of he totally had it coming afterall. Looking further at night it actually gets worse as defecting to the carmarilla is a sin on at least 1,2, 5 and 7. With 2 and 5 being a nightly issue. <br /> <br /> Powers and inner voice is a little better but again I don't think the path will accept becoming a ventrue bootlicker on the possibility you might be get power later on. (Unlikely anyway as the clan just discredited itself in leadership roles vs the ventrue in a truly historic manner). 2 is going to be a problem interacting with other lasombra indefinatly as is 6. 2 might even be enough to cause a wassail as you buckle under a catastrophic internal Paradox.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can see nocturnal redemption being a good option for defectors. If anything it meshes better with carmarilla than Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-23-2022, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T16:16:27-08:00","id":1475265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475225#post1475225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Karos<br /> <br /> I agree with this. I think some Paths (Honorable Accord, Power and Inner Voice especially) would find quite the home in the Camarilla and could possibly create some secret societies around them, even if lip service is still paid to Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honorable accord is theoretically a workable option within carmarilla but is most likely going to cause a full blown wassail due to it definatly being a sin on 1,3,4,5, 8, 10 and probably 6, 7 depending on context. You can't really maintain such a path while being a spineless turncoat and knowing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-22-2022, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T10:46:27-08:00","id":1475334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475265#post1475265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honorable accord is theoretically a workable option within carmarilla but is most likely going to cause a full blown wassail due to it definatly being a sin on 1,3,4,5, 8, 10 and probably 6, 7 depending on context. You can't really maintain such a path while being a spineless turncoat and knowing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you reading the same Honourable accord that I'm reading? It's perfect for a stable undead society like the Camarilla. There's nothing sinful about toeing the Camarilla's line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T12:18:12-08:00","id":1475345,"title":"","content":"I believe Robin's referring to vampires on Honorable Accord switching Sects, not that Honorable Accord couldn't be made to work in the Cam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T17:10:30-08:00","id":1475378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475334#post1475334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you reading the same Honourable accord that I'm reading? It's perfect for a stable undead society like the Camarilla. There's nothing sinful about toeing the Camarilla's line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes exactly, being in the carmarilla would be fine but the damage of betraying Sabbat would be incredibly harrowing for honerable accord. I honestly think I'd suggest a series of roles to prevent outright path collapse if you did it in game. The closest frame of reference for humanity would be the protagonists of a Serbian film, its actually quite hard to imagine how damaging defecting would be. Especially if it'd because you're fleeing the gehenna war","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-23-2022, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T18:37:54-08:00","id":1475384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475378#post1475378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes exactly, being in the carmarilla would be fine but the damage of betraying Sabbat would be incredibly harrowing for honerable accord. I honestly think I'd suggest a series of roles to prevent outright path collapse if you did it in game. The closest frame of reference for humanity would be the protagonists of a Serbian film, its actually quite hard to imagine how damaging defecting would be. Especially if it'd because you're fleeing the gehenna war</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it largely depends on the timeline. If the Sabbat began purging the various Paths and followers of Humanity first, and then Honorable Accord Path followers fled the Sabbat, while it would definitely suck for someone on the Path of Honorable Accord, I don't know that it would cause a Path collapse. After all, they stood with the organization until it stabbed them in the back and the Path doesn't require people to continue to show loyalty to a person or a group after that person/group has already blatantly betrayed and tried to kill the Path follower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T10:45:28-08:00","id":1475543,"title":"","content":"The problem with Sabbat members of the Path adjusting to the Camarilla would be that the Sabbat Honorable Accord is heavily based on the Code of Milan. You can't simply sweep out the Code of Milan with some other system, adjust your loyalties, and be fine. Betraying the Sabbat would be the equivalent of &quot;utter perversion or heinous acts&quot; on the Path of Humanity, and doing so deliberately. Doing so would be equivalent of a normal person suddenly engaging in mass torture and killing of the worst serial killers. Nor would it be the Beast driving them to do that. It would a deliberate choice.<br /> <br /> As an ST, at the very least I'd rule that there is no Path check, but immediate loss of several Path levels. I might even lower their Conscience and Self-Control.<br /> <br /> And after the betrayal happens, realistically how can they continue their adherence to a Path which they betrayed on a fundamental level? After all, aren't they themselves now among the Dishonorable? Which means they can't ever NOT associate with the dishonorable. Is it now impossible for them to ever increase their rating above 7? Yes, they can somehow adjust their following of the old Sabbat Honorable Accord with some new Honorable Accord variant that is aligned with the Camarilla, but nevertheless they are dealing with the fact that they committed a Path sin equivalent to a human person voluntarily committing mass torture and killing. You just can't move beyond that. You've told your Beast that the very foundations of your Path is now open to negotiation, and it is going to begin pushing you to your limits. Once you've made the ultimate betrayal, you can't tell yourself &quot;No, I would never do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honorable Accord would be a Path that is theoretically acceptable in the Camarilla, as it uses the Virtues of Conscience and Self-Control, and would lead to behavior that is consistent with Camarilla society and the Masquerade. But that would be an entirely separate variant of the Path of Honorable Accord found in the Sabbat which internalizes the Code of Milan. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> Robin said, any Sabbat member with it who defects is effectively choosing to abandon the Path. If they were going to do that, it'd just be best for them to convert to an alternate Path as it'd be hard for them to ever say they could become &quot;honorable&quot; again.<br /> <br /> =<br /> I think most Sabbat Paths would be incompatible with Camarilla society. The only ones that would be acceptable would be those that would seem to fit in with current society and not threaten the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Despite the Path of Caine being based on Conviction &amp; Instinct, few of its &quot;sins&quot; would require behavior disruptive of the Camarilla's goals. There probably would be certain changes from the Path practiced in the Sabbat from one practiced in the Camarilla, but that could easily be explained by an discovery of &quot;lore&quot; or an &quot;improved pedagogy.&quot; A few defecting Lasombra might follow such a Path.<br /> <br /> The original Path of Harmony using Conscience could probably transfer to the Camarilla as well. But its adherents would mostly be Gangrel living away from cities, and thus ignore most of vampire society anyway. They'd just be transferring their allegiance from the Sabbat hierarchy to the Inner Circle. But that isn't a sin, especially if the Sabbat ever did anything like attempting to exterminate all followers of the Path. However, there's probably no Lasombra on this path.<br /> <br /> A Path of Honorable Accord independent of the Sabbat/Code of Milan could coexist within the Camarilla, but for reasons already explained, I don't think any Sabbat already on this Path could actually defect.<br /> <br /> The Path of Power and the Inner Voice could conceivably work within the Camarilla, but there's two problems as I see it. First, it works best for former Sabbat who were relatively young and had not achieved much Power yet. For older vampires who had progressed along the Path and gathered power within the Sabbat, defecting to the Camarilla would be admitting several Path violations that would erode Path ratings and empower the Beast. Secondly, while nothing on the Path would seem to be disruptive of the Masquerade, it's probably intensely politically destabilizing. Every domain which has members of this Path would cause even more trouble for the Prince or other leaders. The Sabbat could handle such chaos. Chaos was normal for a Sabbat domain, and it had various methods of channeling dissent and ambition like Monomacy. The Camarilla wants stability. Camarilla vampires are equally ambitious as Sabbat ones, but at least they are not on a Path that requires them to never admit defeat and keep pushing things in order to not violate their ethics. They can retreat and plot again without empowering their Beast. So in fact, I don't think this would make a good Path in the Camarilla despite its surface appearance. Young, ambitious Lasombra defectors from the Sabbat could follow this Path, but I suspect as they cause problems for Princes and other Camarilla elders in the subsequent years, they'd slowly be purged.<br /> <br /> So I think only a few Paths could potentially work in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> As I said on another thread, if you want more Lasombra, the best thing is to just increase the number of existing Lasombra antitribu in the Camarilla. Maybe cause some things to happen that would justify a Lasombra AT on the Inner Circle and give them a Justicar. Maybe Montana succeeds in destroying Gratiano, and the Sabbat implodes in Civil War, raising the Lasombra AT's prestige and numbers in the Camarilla? Or your own ideas. But that won't do much to spread Paths within the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T12:16:08-08:00","id":1475674,"title":"","content":"For the matter of the Honorable Accord, I think context can facilitate transition for at least some members without breaking many or any precept of the Path at all, because Code of Milan or not, it isn't the Path of Following the Sabbat:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_article-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to uphold all the precepts of your group (in most cases, the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sabbat\" target=\"_blank\">Sabbat</a>).</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>The group the character identifies with may be the clan or pack, not necessarily the Sabbat as a whole.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to show hospitality to your allies.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>Depends on whom the character may consider allies.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Associating with the dishonorable.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>A number of member could see the new Sabbat as ignoble here, depending on how that vampire sees the recent Sabbat decisions.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to participate in your groups' <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Auctoritas_Ritae\" target=\"_blank\">rites</a>.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>It is far more linked to clan and pack than the sect as a whole.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Disobeying your leader.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>Wasn't it an order from the Amici? How do you chose between two leaders?</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Failing to protect your allies.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>See 9.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Placing personal concerns over duty.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>Only a sin if the vampire is acting out of cowardice and not out of an order or a sense of duty to the clan.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Showing cowardice.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>Betrayal or defection aren't the same a cowardice, especially if the betrayal in question puts you in great personal danger, which happened to some.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Killing without reason.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>Not a thing in this context. They either didn't need to, or had a reason.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_article-table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\">Breaking your word or oath; failing to honor an agreement.</td> <td class=\"text_table_article-table_td\"><b>Most Sabbat members have oaths for their packs, not the sept as a whole, and even then it doesn't mean an oath can't be revoked. It would be a complicated thing to do, but is feasible.</b></td> </tr> </table></div> </div> </div> </div>All in all, I think it is quite feasible that some Path followers managed to defect without much trouble. Maybe risking a dot or two, but as long as they manage to avoid or justify the level 1 (worst sin possible), they would be able to make the transition. That isn't to say that it would work every time or even on most of them, but I don't see it as being an instant Path Collapse either. Context, as always, matters.<br /> <br /> But for the OP question, it is unlikely that the defection will affect the Camarilla to such extent.<br /> <br /> Thing is, Roads were a thing. Options to Humanity existed in a more amenable way even, far before the current Paths were invented. Many Elders still personally remember them, some still follow them, and finding about them isn't that hard for Ancilla or Neonates. Yet the Camarilla take the decision to excise them and focus exclusively on Humanity, their arguments, opinions and the reasons for this still stand.<br /> <br /> Now, it doesn't mean that finding Paths among the Cam is impossible, or that the newcomers won't keep their Paths when possible. It depends on your take on the whole matter already, because the game never had a hard stance on how rare or common they were in the Cam to begin with beyond <i>somewhat rare</i>.<br /> <br /> In my view it is unlikely that the Cam will see with good eyes Path followers that are too open about it, or the active spread of Paths. But they're also unlikely to outright forbid and hunt down such vampires, the same way they never hunted down Noddists just for being so. Problematic Path Followers are bound to be found red-handed anyway by the usual laws, non-problematic ones are better off not being forced to betray their beliefs and risk Wassail.<br /> <br /> What is a problem with modern Paths is that Humanity <b>is</b> the most stable one for the newly Embraced as it is more intuitive for them. I see a lot of people arguing that Humanity isn't the best Path for the Cam, but they usually ignore the many aspects it covers, and the first one is to keep Kindred from going nuts from the get go. There's no need for indoctrination and tests, there's no need to risk Wassail in the learning process, you just say that most things most people learn all their lives to be wrong are still wrong and that's it.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Path followers exist in the Cam already and will increase simply because most defectors in a Path won't change at first. They may spread a little, but in a short term it wont go far, especially when you add to it just how hard it is to switch to a Path. In time it may come to change, but I don't think it really will do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T13:08:40-08:00","id":1475678,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth saying; as much as breaking your word is the Honourable accord equivalent to doing the TheSickestOfUnspeakablyFuckedUpSickShit while on humanity, you can do TheSickestOfUnspeakablyFuckedUpSickShit on humanity and not wight yourself right away for doing it. Like, the rules aren't exactly clear, but assuming you've got a path rating at around 5, it'd be egregious if you lost more than 3 dots of Honourable accord for it. Your path rating isn't how well you follow the path, it's how much your path gives you strength to resist the beast. Switching sects is a heavy hit, but circumstances willing it's not an automatic Wight maker. Affirm for yourself new bonds and you'll have new strength to resist the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T15:06:40-08:00","id":1475684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475674#post1475674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the matter of the Honorable Accord, I think context can facilitate transition for at least some members without breaking many or any precept of the Path at all, because Code of Milan or not, it isn't the Path of Following the Sabbat<br /> <br /> All in all, I think it is quite feasible that some Path followers managed to defect without much trouble. Maybe risking a dot or two, but as long as they manage to avoid or justify the level 1 (worst sin possible), they would be able to make the transition. That isn't to say that it would work every time or even on most of them, but I don't see it as being an instant Path Collapse either. Context, as always, matters.<br /> <br /> But for the OP question, it is unlikely that the defection will affect the Camarilla to such extent.<br /> <br /> Thing is, Roads were a thing. Options to Humanity existed in a more amenable way even, far before the current Paths were invented. Many Elders still personally remember them, some still follow them, and finding about them isn't that hard for Ancilla or Neonates. Yet the Camarilla take the decision to excise them and focus exclusively on Humanity, their arguments, opinions and the reasons for this still stand.<br /> <br /> Now, it doesn't mean that finding Paths among the Cam is impossible, or that the newcomers won't keep their Paths when possible. It depends on your take on the whole matter already, because the game never had a hard stance on how rare or common they were in the Cam to begin with beyond <i>somewhat rare</i>.<br /> <br /> In my view it is unlikely that the Cam will see with good eyes Path followers that are too open about it, or the active spread of Paths. But they're also unlikely to outright forbid and hunt down such vampires, the same way they never hunted down Noddists just for being so. Problematic Path Followers are bound to be found red-handed anyway by the usual laws, non-problematic ones are better off not being forced to betray their beliefs and risk Wassail.<br /> <br /> What is a problem with modern Paths is that Humanity <b>is</b> the most stable one for the newly Embraced as it is more intuitive for them. I see a lot of people arguing that Humanity isn't the best Path for the Cam, but they usually ignore the many aspects it covers, and the first one is to keep Kindred from going nuts from the get go. There's no need for indoctrination and tests, there's no need to risk Wassail in the learning process, you just say that most things most people learn all their lives to be wrong are still wrong and that's it.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Path followers exist in the Cam already and will increase simply because most defectors in a Path won't change at first. They may spread a little, but in a short term it wont go far, especially when you add to it just how hard it is to switch to a Path. In time it may come to change, but I don't think it really will do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are certainly interesting counterpoint but they sounds more like rationlizations of path breach than anything For example 5-9 relies on getting real flacky who counts as ally and its incredibly unlikely that you're on the path without at least some oaths, incidently oaths definatly arnt circumventable-thats why they're oaths rather than a general agreement. It also relies heavily on a clan first approach to the Path, something which isnt really the case i how its historically been written especially considering huge chunks of the defectors would be (correctly) perceived as spineless hypocrites<br /> <br /> Its also probably worth noting if you're on a path and looking to circumvent the rules with rationalizations I'd frown very heavily on it from a gm perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-02-2022, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T15:14:26-08:00","id":1475686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475678#post1475678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's worth saying; as much as breaking your word is the Honourable accord equivalent to doing the TheSickestOfUnspeakablyFuckedUpSickShit while on humanity, you can do TheSickestOfUnspeakablyFuckedUpSickShit on humanity and not wight yourself right away for doing it. Like, the rules aren't exactly clear, but assuming you've got a path rating at around 5, it'd be egregious if you lost more than 3 dots of Honourable accord for it. Your path rating isn't how well you follow the path, it's how much your path gives you strength to resist the beast. Switching sects is a heavy hit, but circumstances willing it's not an automatic Wight maker. Affirm for yourself new bonds and you'll have new strength to resist the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but its very hard on a personal level to walk away from that level of sin. Level one sins are acts of sh<br /> Soul destroying horror .even if you don't Wassail you're going be incredibly messed up after and completly discredited your ethical guards against the beast.<br /> As I recall correctly you don't auto Wassail if you drop to zero on a path I think you just jump back onto Humanity 1.<br /> <br /> Edit-removed example of humanity one sin, apologies my sensibilities are rather jaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-02-2022, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T17:01:24-08:00","id":1475690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475684#post1475684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are certainly interesting counterpoint but they sounds more like rationlizations of path breach than any</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that and agree, hence saying that it wouldn't work most of the time.<br /> <br /> Basically, given that this is a Path, a lot would depend on the personal perspective of the follower. So we would have four kinds of followers here:<br /> <br /> A) Loyal to the Sabbat to the bitter end, they won't defect, period;<br /> <br /> B) Defectors that fear the Gehenna War and admit such. They would take a heavy toll and possibly have to either abandon the Path or seek redemption somehow in their new sect, and would probably cut ties with the clan (as they perceive the clan as dishonorable);<br /> <br /> C) Those who fool themselves by rationalizing the deed with any or all the things I gave as examples. Depending on the ST and on the circumstances they may have a somewhat easier time resisting the initial hit (although I would actually favor those recognizing and seeking redemption), but over time they're likely to really go into the downward spiral towards Wassail as they don't recognize their own failings in this Path;<br /> <br /> D) Some for whom my arguments really hold, those would be the stable Path followers in the Cam. Yes, it seems like rationalization, but for some it would simply be true. Especially given how the Amici and the Lasombra work, so some members would have loyalty to the clan instead of the Sabbat <i>on purpose</i>.<br /> <br /> How many would be in each situation is up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T21:53:04-08:00","id":1475710,"title":"","content":"While I think there are variations of the Path of the Honorable Accord that would work well in the Camarilla, I don't think most adherents of the Path in the Sabbat could defect. The books make it clear, in almost every edition of VtM (I don't know V5 so I can't comment on that), that the Sabbat Path of the Honorable Accord is intrinsically tied to the Code of Milan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Players Guide to Sabbat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is little more than a code of conduct which serves to keep some semblance of order in a very chaotic sect. In fact, those on this Path are often referred to as followers of the Code. The Path is spelled out in a book called the Code of Milan.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guide to Sabbat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although the original chivalric precepts upon which this path bases itself fell out of use by the Renaissance, some members of the Sabbat adopted similar philosophies, and the path adopted the Code of Milan after the first Sabbat civil war. Sabbat followers of the path turned their loyalty to the idealism of the sect and letter of the code, in the process acquiring the moniker \u201cfollowers of the Code.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 Corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Honorable Accord grew out of bygone nights, as vampires of the Dark Ages grappled with the problems of human morality by finding a harsh and unyielding code of conduct to replace the ethics of mankind. Sabbat followers of the Path turned their loyalty to the idealism of the Sect and the letter of the Code of Milan, in the process acquiring the moniker \u201cfollowers of the Code.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Code of Milan is pretty clear in its loyalties to the Sabbat. Here are some of the relevant precepts of the Code.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Code of Milan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat shall remain united in its support of the sect's Regent.<br /> <br /> All Sabbat must put the good of the sect before their own personal needs, despite all costs.<br /> <br /> All Sabbat shall protect one another from the enemies of the sect.<br /> <br /> All sect members shall protect Sabbat territory from all other powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see how any Sabbat on the Path of Honorable Code can defect to the Camarilla and possibly remain on the Path. Now there may be some rare Sabbat on this Path that do not use the Code of Milan as its basis. They might be able to continue on their Path after defecting. But they should not be representative of the vast majority of the Path.<br /> <br /> Trying to find wriggle room for justification for defection is something that lawyers and sophists can do. It's not behavior that people generally associate with &quot;honorable&quot; people.<br /> <br /> If you are at the point where you point to members of the Sabbat as not being &quot;true&quot; Sabbat, you don't defect to the Camarilla. You remain true to your ideals, proclaim them as false Sabbat and attempt to rally the &quot;true&quot; Sabbat while destroying the apostates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T22:14:12-08:00","id":1475713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475710#post1475710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are at the point where you point to members of the Sabbat as not being &quot;true&quot; Sabbat, you don't defect to the Camarilla. You remain true to your ideals, proclaim them as false Sabbat and attempt to rally the &quot;true&quot; Sabbat while destroying the apostates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, again on the basis of personal circumstances.<br /> <br /> Now, IIRC, there was no Regent when the Defection occurred. The sect was in turmoil and many aspects of it that were just as important or even more than fighting the Ancients, depending on one's views, were being dropped by it.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat shall remain united under the Regent, but there is no Regent. The Sabbat must put the good of the sect before personal needs, but was throwing the good of the sect away. The Sabbat shall protect one another from their enemies, but they became their own enemies hunting one another in the name of the crusade. All Sabbat territory shall be protected, but the territory was abandoned.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the Code can we truly call the NuSabbat the Sabbat at all? Is this the Sabbat the followers of Honorable Accord believe in? And if the Sabbat is no more, does it makes sense to just throw your allegiance towards the ragtag band of zealots that proclaim themselves the true Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Such are not just questions for lawyers and sophists. They're questions for the Path Follower to answer themselves. And by the very nature of a Path, the judge of the matter is ultimately the follower themselves. One may be incapable of really believing in Honorable Accord without the Sabbat, others may be just fooling themselves, paying heed to the sophists but bowing to their cowardice. But other follower may have the same unwavering conviction that this mockery isn't no Sabbat, and that the Camarilla isn't their enemy anymore, maybe even the only hope now to rebuild the true Sabbat in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T23:06:00-08:00","id":1475715,"title":"","content":"I imagine going by the code of Milan for someone on the honourable accord is more like agreeing to the terms of conditions on software than keeping your word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T01:09:42-08:00","id":1475722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475715#post1475715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine going by the code of Milan for someone on the honourable accord is more like agreeing to the terms of conditions on software than keeping your word.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's almost certainly not what honerable accord is like at all. It's a sacred oath and a deeply held conviction you can't flip flop on it anymore than a humanity vampire could smash a neo nazis head in with a claw hammer because &quot;he had it coming.&quot;. A paths ultimate objective is to guard against the beast and the beast wants you to rationalise breaches....its partly how you degenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T01:29:08-08:00","id":1475724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475713#post1475713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, again on the basis of personal circumstances.<br /> <br /> Now, IIRC, there was no Regent when the Defection occurred. The sect was in turmoil and many aspects of it that were just as important or even more than fighting the Ancients, depending on one's views, were being dropped by it.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat shall remain united under the Regent, but there is no Regent. The Sabbat must put the good of the sect before personal needs, but was throwing the good of the sect away. The Sabbat shall protect one another from their enemies, but they became their own enemies hunting one another in the name of the crusade. All Sabbat territory shall be protected, but the territory was abandoned.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the Code can we truly call the NuSabbat the Sabbat at all? Is this the Sabbat the followers of Honorable Accord believe in? And if the Sabbat is no more, does it makes sense to just throw your allegiance towards the ragtag band of zealots that proclaim themselves the true Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Such are not just questions for lawyers and sophists. They're questions for the Path Follower to answer themselves. And by the very nature of a Path, the judge of the matter is ultimately the follower themselves. One may be incapable of really believing in Honorable Accord without the Sabbat, others may be just fooling themselves, paying heed to the sophists but bowing to their cowardice. But other follower may have the same unwavering conviction that this mockery isn't no Sabbat, and that the Camarilla isn't their enemy anymore, maybe even the only hope now to rebuild the true Sabbat in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again these sound very much like rationalizations, with honerable accord I suspect they'd rather go down with the ship in the same sense I'd sincerly rather die irl than commit a rank humanity 1 and multiple sins as well even under extreme duress as I suspect most people would. We can all fill on how we'd react being asked to do a level 1 even under coercion or duress.<br /> <br /> &quot;The current Sabbat is unworthy of your loyalty.&quot;<br /> &quot;It does not matter. The oath was given.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you really want to throw your unlife away for a lost cause?&quot;<br /> &quot;It was never my life to throw away.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact thinking on it a knight would probably go out of their way to restore and save the Sabbat rather than bail. <br /> <br /> I can see three ways can see a credible path member in the carmarilla without taking massive path damage is if they're lying and just trying to get close to a lasombra defector for termination. Which would actually be a pretty cool plot.<br /> The second I could see older road of Kings vampires adopting a psuado honerable accord but this would be covergant evolution rather than &quot;hey I'm a Sabbat honerable accord defector.&quot;. Thirdly I could see would be if the Sabbat directly betrayed you which might work but I'd imagine that'd still.cause a crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-04-2022, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T11:49:42-08:00","id":1475742,"title":"","content":"If those who Sabbat who follow the Path of Honorable Accord cannot tolerate the &quot;NuSabbat&quot; as real Sabbat, then the choice is simple. Either engage in a Fourth Sabbat Civil War to defend their ideals and defeat their internal enemy, or somehow reconcile their Path with the NuSabbat accordingly. (The end result of the civil war might be the defeat of one side versus the other, or the permanent division into two warring sects. Past civil wars did last for many decades or even centuries). Perhaps going into some kind &quot;exile&quot; remaining loyal to a Sabbat that no longer exists and perhaps rebuild the sect. Different followers of the Path might justify all three. But defection to the Camarilla seems pretty impossible IF you want to remain on the Path. (I have no problem with someone abandoning the Path because he comes to some personal crisis and decides he can't be part of the Sabbat anymore, but he'd have to start a new path.)<br /> <br /> The only way members on that Path could defect to the Camarilla is pretty much to abandon the Path entirely and adopt another one. I can't see them adjusting the Path to some other means (like a variation of the Path that some Camarilla archons might be using) because they've already committed treason and dishonor and pretty much destroyed the foundations of their Path. If they commit the ultimate betrayal of their Path once, they can do it again. It'll no longer be effective at holding back the Beast. It'd be a mockery of the Path to betray its foundations, but somehow remain on it constantly justifying your original betrayal by remaining within the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> An otherwise &quot;honorable&quot; Sabbat who is NOT on the Path can defect without the blowback that comes with committing sins of that Path. He'll be seen as dishonorable, but won't suffer Path violations. (And as I said earlier, there might be a few Path followers who were following some extremely rare variant in the Sabbat that did not incorporate the Code of Milan in it. I would still think betrayal of the sect while remaining on the Path extremely unlikely, but conceivably there could be some really strange version that squares the circle. It's just extremely unlikely.)<br /> <br /> The thing about a code of Honor, is that it gives its followers respect by its society because it commits its adherents to certain absolutes. Death before dishonor. A follower of the Code of Milan might justify many things, but betrayal of his sect by joining the Camarilla isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> The captain must go down with his ship. The samurai who is ordered by his lord to commit seppuku must kill himself. The knight bravely charges into a doomed attack because his king commanded it. That's what people with &quot;honor&quot; do. (Sometimes &quot;honor&quot; demands strange things. If you're a soldier you are not suppose to run, but if the unit is being wiped out and you are given the regimental colors to protect them, you're then expected to escape so the dishonor of having your colors captured doesn't happen. So we're not talking about absolutes here, just what the people in that situation consider the honorable thing to do. And of course, different societies can have different ideas of what honor entails.)<br /> <br /> Certainly there are captains, samurais, knights, soldiers, etc. who don't do the &quot;honorable&quot; thing that their society demands. But they won't be seen as honorable. They'll be seen as dishonorable.<br /> <br /> Because of their failure at the Battle of Midway, Admiral Yamaguchi and Captain Kaku decided that honor demanded them to go down with the IJN Hiryu because they had failed their men and Emperor and they wanted to atone for that failure. Whether that was truly needed by the dictates of Japanese honor is debatable. But one thing they did not do is defect to the Americans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7gSwpCahZq4\" data-code=\"7gSwpCahZq4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7gSwpCahZq4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> \u200bAt this point, I think I said everything I mean about this scenario. I understand <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> thinks differently. While I would be willing to listen to a PC attempting to justify his Sabbat Path of Honorable Accord Lasombra defecting to the Camarilla and keeping on his Path, I can't think of anything that would cause me to say &quot;Yeah, that works.&quot; But I always remember to never say &quot;always&quot; or &quot;never&quot;. I might be surprised by the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T15:24:30-08:00","id":1475745,"title":"","content":"While we're all pontificating on the specifics here (since everyone seems to agree that a vampire on Honorable Accord switching Sects would be a big deal regardless)...<br /> <br /> I can't help but feel Honorable Accord is being held to standard Humanity and the other Paths aren't here. No Path is constructed so flimsily that you can't screw up. None of them are written such that even if you commit the worst of its sins, you can't find you way back to the teachings of the Path. That's not in the rules, and that's no in the descriptions (of Paths in general or Honorable Accord specifically).<br /> <br /> It seems like one of the disconnects is how many violations switching side would be. Robin seems to be taking a more maximal approach (one I don't think meshes with the rules that well) of rolling a lot for every step of the process leading to a very high likelihood of falling off the Path completely into wight-dom. monteparnas seems to be taking the more minimal approach (perhaps more in the letter of the rules but perhaps a bit too lenient at the same time) where even if it's a level 1 sin, that's what you roll and you either end up at your level or down one dot at the end of the day.<br /> <br /> Vampire minds are human enough to engage with the rationalizations, frailties, and so on that allow us to do things we know are wrong, without believing we're horrible people for it. Joining a Path doesn't get rid of that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T01:15:50-08:00","id":1475769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475745#post1475745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're all pontificating on the specifics here (since everyone seems to agree that a vampire on Honorable Accord switching Sects would be a big deal regardless)...<br /> <br /> I can't help but feel Honorable Accord is being held to standard Humanity and the other Paths aren't here. No Path is constructed so flimsily that you can't screw up. None of them are written such that even if you commit the worst of its sins, you can't find you way back to the teachings of the Path. That's not in the rules, and that's no in the descriptions (of Paths in general or Honorable Accord specifically).<br /> <br /> It seems like one of the disconnects is how many violations switching side would be. Robin seems to be taking a more maximal approach (one I don't think meshes with the rules that well) of rolling a lot for every step of the process leading to a very high likelihood of falling off the Path completely into wight-dom. monteparnas seems to be taking the more minimal approach (perhaps more in the letter of the rules but perhaps a bit too lenient at the same time) where even if it's a level 1 sin, that's what you roll and you either end up at your level or down one dot at the end of the day.<br /> <br /> Vampire minds are human enough to engage with the rationalizations, frailties, and so on that allow us to do things we know are wrong, without believing we're horrible people for it. Joining a Path doesn't get rid of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its more that the sins are a good point of referance to my point. We can easily look at the tenants and the same issue emerges:<br /> <br /> -Always keep your word and honor your agreements.<br /> Never show cowardice. Overcome your fears.<br /> -Duty comes before personal matters.<br /> -Treat fairly and equitably with those of station. Conversely, the dishonorable are beneath your contempt.<br /> Always repay your debts.<br /> -Support your comrades-at-arms in all things, except where they counsel treachery.<br /> <br /> <br /> The last one really hammers home the issue. My point isn't that defecting is impossible its that defecting is incredibly unlikely, it's the equivelant of a Redemption aiding a nephandi and sincerly embracing their outlook or Night engaging in extended humanitarian efforts without darker motives. It's not merely a sin it's a direct contradiction of your fundamental nature.<br /> <br /> Edit-thinking on it cathari which is apparently (and bizzarely) the main path in v5 sabbat is probably a way better candidate for defection. Being selfish hedonistic assholes seem more geared towards treason especially in v5 were youre apparently expected to run around in a feral pack constantly engaging in asymmetric warfare for the greater good.<br /> <br /> Nocturnal/redemption is probably the best option as well. It's actually pretty badly suited to the Sabbat when you read up on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-04-2022, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T02:47:27-08:00","id":1475770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475769#post1475769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Treat fairly and equitably with those of station. Conversely, the dishonorable are beneath your contempt.<br /> -Support your comrades-at-arms in all things, except where they counsel treachery.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, these seem to support monteparnas's position and not yours.<br /> <br /> Honorable Accord is not Lawful Stupid. If the Sabbat has a whole has become dishonorable, and treacherous, these ethics would say that the right thing to do is to leave this diminished and failed Sabbat behind. Honorable Accord's ethics don't support the idea that its followers would go down with sinking ship of betrayal and lies. According to these ethics is absolutely matters if the Sabbat remains worthy. <br /> <br /> If anything, this says the opposite of what you're saying. It sets up a clear set of conditions where the ethics of the Path support switching Sect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T05:14:09-08:00","id":1475771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475770#post1475770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If anything, these seem to support monteparnas's position and not yours.<br /> <br /> Honorable Accord is not Lawful Stupid. If the Sabbat has a whole has become dishonorable, and treacherous, these ethics would say that the right thing to do is to leave this diminished and failed Sabbat behind. Honorable Accord's ethics don't support the idea that its followers would go down with sinking ship of betrayal and lies. According to these ethics is absolutely matters if the Sabbat remains worthy. <br /> <br /> If anything, this says the opposite of what you're saying. It sets up a clear set of conditions where the ethics of the Path support switching Sect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it really has, it's dumber certainly but if anything its more martial orientated, the objections to it from an honerable accord perspective would be linked to its practical failures rather than ethical. The Sabbat hasn't betrayed its cause its just a complete failure at them. The lasombra by contrast are complete spineless turncoats by the paths outlook. They're not fleeing because they're morally incorrect they're fleeing because they don't fancy their odds <br /> <br /> Agreed hence why they can't just jump ship because of sects 'alignment shift' if we're using d&amp;d terminology.<br /> <br /> Actually they kind of do, nothing written about the paths indicates a willingness to flee or turncoat in the face of failure. If anything dying for a lost cause or to save face is probably approved off wereasTreachery is incredibly frowned upon.<br /> <br /> I'm not convinced it does. I can't see anything which would allow someone to circumvent a defection to a enemy organization in the face of failure and doom. If anything that seems like the sort of situation were the paths beliefs are put to the test. Which is why they're beliefs and not just ideas which sound nice but might not back up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-04-2022, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T12:52:22-08:00","id":1475795,"title":"","content":"This starts to feel less about if those following Honorable Accord could move to the Camarilla and more about particular clashing stances on the V5 Sabbat plot, with this discussion as proxy (with &quot;no, you can't, it should be plot and mechanically impossible and auto wight whoever tries, they should have to stay and fight for the sabbat&quot; feeling basically like a note of that if it was acknowledged they could, it would be like agreeing the V5 plot was okay, therefore it can't be agreed with to be possible. And I say this as someone that is pretty solidly on record as disliking almost everything V5 pretty thoroughly. And of course there's what feels like a flip side of &quot;well paths/this specific path are bad anyway, it's great that players can't have them in V5, and your path requiring you to now die, or auto wighting you if you don't is what you deserve for being on this one&quot;.) Ultimately, as far as V20 (the system being referred to for use), from a using the actual mechanics perspective, it boils down to at most two path checks for the decision at the time from even a stringent a reading of conscience/conviction checks, and thereby at worst, losing a couple of path dots. You don't actually keep making endless path checks for a particular act once you've done the particular act, that's not how that works. Nor does a single act (for example, defecting) require multiple checks for every single potential morality violation it includes. That's not how that works either.<br /> <br /> As for griping about something being rationalization? Again, that's part of how the check works. Part of making the check includes the idea that you are able to justify the transgression to yourself and come to terms with it. Those are almost actual verbatim words from the description of what a morality check is. The game we are talking about, as long as the theoretically Honourable Accord follower has a rating of more than, let's say 4, would entirely allow for the notion of defecting path followers being able to both defect and keep their path, even if they fail two path checks (and again, by actual rules, it's really just one act, and thus one check, even making it two checks is already going to a land of overinterpreting the rules here, as though V20's particular take on morality does not align with how some people want the take on it to be), without now being 2 more away from wight-dom. And it's not for certain they would fail them checks at that.<br /> <br /> For me, my perspective here comes down to &quot;how would this feel as a player in a campaign if this happened.&quot; If the ST goes to me &quot;guess what, the Sabbat is now completely different than you knew and pledged to, and in fact as a sect is proclaiming you and everything you believe in to have been wrong and casting you out/wanting you dead.&quot; Then it feels entirely fair to go &quot;Well then, if the Sabbat has betrayed me and become a thing of dishonour, my own ethos allows for the possibility of renouncing it as far as if the entire group has become dishonourable, which I thus do.&quot; And that an ST reply of &quot;Alright, that does fit within your worldview as far as you've explained it, but it also feels like a rationalization to justify something you know is wrong, make a path check for renouncing the sect for reflecting how much you really believe it and how much it is regardless a measure of spiritual degeneration that you're crashing into, and maybe a follow up one for actually joining a different sect full out.&quot; would feel like a fair enough response.<br /> <br /> A response instead of &quot;No! You have to either keep being Sabbat and probably die or roll and fail path checks until you become a wight!&quot; is the ST being kind of a jerk. Like picture telling a player something like that. And sure, an ST in the first place going &quot;you know that sect you built your entire character around? That sect has deemed you and everything you believe in completely invalid&quot;, is pretty bad too, but allowing for a varying response within worldview that comes at potential cost is still better handled than the alternative. I have regardless on an anecdotal level found there are games that do things like want to use V5 plot elements but still keep the V20 system, sizable games even, so pondering this whole thing in a &quot;what would actually feel fair to a player on a level of a game people play&quot; level still feels worth considering.<br /> <br /> Also, if we're talking V20, I know it's been noted before, but to remind, Honorable Accord is specifically named out as a path that is noted as being followed by &quot;a rare few Ventrue Elders&quot;, and otherwise apparently being a thing some Archons and Alastors follow as well, as far as the Camarilla. The V20 take on Honourable Accord is less &quot;this was created by the Sabbat&quot; and more &quot;people on Chivalry/Kings in either sect evolved their beliefs into this Path, it's more popular in the Sabbat because the Sabbat is the sect that does paths as its deal&quot;. For an Honorable Accord follower who has just been betrayed by their entire sect, that whole thing being the case is certainly something that might get some notice for &quot;well perhaps then I could find a way to exist in that sect now and maintain my honour.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's otherwise a deeply punitive element to this discussion that feels off. Like it's actively looking for ways to be harsher than even the game actually encourages reading its take on things to be and it's worth taking a step back and remembering that this is also a game people play, not just a narrative to be discussed. A take that boils down to &quot;well, you picked the wrong page in the Choose Your Own Adventure with no indication it would be, so now you have to die&quot; doesn't feel great for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  quick grammar thing 03-05-2022, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T15:04:46-08:00","id":1475801,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a><br /> <br /> I'm really not sure what you're trying to get at. Nobody is saying that someone on Honorable Accord would find quitting their current Sect easy. Just that it isn't something in the realms of unthinkable actions for them. The Path is clear that its followers loyalty is conditional. There are lines where those they are loyal to can cross, and members of the Path would consider it a negation of their duties to that individual/group. That doesn't mean they don't have to roll for a sin or two. That doesn't mean it's easy (esp. with the Sabbat and the Viniculum). It just means if a situation arises where the Sabbat as a whole as devolved into dishonor and treachery, the Path doesn't say, &quot;it doesn't matter, you keep at it knowing it will be your doom.&quot; Yes, the Path does say fight to your doom if your comrades stay loyal and honorable. But the contention is that the events of where the Sabbat is going could lead to that no longer being true in the eyes of some Path members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T02:38:49-08:00","id":1475887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475801#post1475801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a><br /> <br /> I'm really not sure what you're trying to get at. Nobody is saying that someone on Honorable Accord would find quitting their current Sect easy. Just that it isn't something in the realms of unthinkable actions for them. The Path is clear that its followers loyalty is conditional. There are lines where those they are loyal to can cross, and members of the Path would consider it a negation of their duties to that individual/group. That doesn't mean they don't have to roll for a sin or two. That doesn't mean it's easy (esp. with the Sabbat and the Viniculum). It just means if a situation arises where the Sabbat as a whole as devolved into dishonor and treachery, the Path doesn't say, &quot;it doesn't matter, you keep at it knowing it will be your doom.&quot; Yes, the Path does say fight to your doom if your comrades stay loyal and honorable. But the contention is that the events of where the Sabbat is going could lead to that no longer being true in the eyes of some Path members.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I get that bit, my observation is that a path member is not only incredibly unlikely to defect but is also incredibly unlikely to even consider doing so. Nothing about the philosophy, sins or outlook even seems like it would even be considered outside of extreme personal situations.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong?<br /> <br /> The part which I don't get is how has the Sabbat devolved into treachery? the recent fluff indicates its more unified and focused on war than ever. It just isn't very good at it. Cathari and power seem more likely to object since youre a twitchy psycho whose not really allowed to engage in the accumulation of power or sin outside of hyper niche contexts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-06-2022, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T07:02:39-08:00","id":1475895,"title":"","content":"So far as I understand it, the Sabbat basically said, &quot;Okay, all that talk about killing Antediluvians and stopped Gehenna? Well, it's go time! Time to fight or die, sink or swim.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Lasombra (and others but mostly the Lasombra) said, &quot;... naaaaah, I don't really want to die fighting the elders. Turns out this whole thing was just a LARP and we're gonna go join the Camarilla. Deuces!&quot;<br /> <br /> I have a hard time seeing vampires on the Path of Honorable Accord abandoning their faction, their allies and their very raison d'etre because they don't want to die. That mostly goes against all of the Path's precepts. Now at an individual level there would certainly be a few, but I imagine the vast majority of the Path followers would have been on the first red-eye flight to the Middle East to go fight. That would be my guess as to why there aren't any left - they all went to bravely face their Final Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-06-2022, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T08:55:19-08:00","id":1475899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475742#post1475742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're a soldier you are not suppose to run, but if the unit is being wiped out and you are given the regimental colors to protect them, you're then expected to escape so the dishonor of having your colors captured doesn't happen. So we're not talking about absolutes here, just what the people in that situation consider the honorable thing to do. And of course, different societies can have different ideas of what honor entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's my whole point, even letting aside the whole fact that this interpretation of honor didn't actually worked quite like that in the real world in the times they're purported to have worked (both Samurais and Knights only became that &quot;honorable&quot; during the romantic period of their downfall, and captains do not sink with the ship).<br /> <br /> Despite the general description, Path Followers (for any Path) are individuals that exist in specific contexts and have specific outlooks. They're not the generic description of the Path, they're their individual ideas of what the Path means.<br /> <br /> \u200bSorry, but my problem here is that you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> are assuming too absolute interpretations for the Path. At no point I'm saying, and in this I repeat myself, that any particular proportion of the followers would do this or that, much less that a significant number would defect. But to think that absolutely none or only a unique PC would do so is, to me, completely unreasonable.<br /> <br /> Followers of the Honorable Accord have complex loyalties. They're loyal to Pack, Clan, Sect, and other people depending on personal history and context, not to say the Code itself. What to say if some of those loyalties clash? If you think Sect takes precedence, that's <b><u>YOUR</u></b> interpretation, only. The individual follower has a tough decision to make, or maybe not so tough. Some will chose sect without a second thought, and some will ditch it with the same ease. Not out of cowardice or disloyalty, but out of loyalty to other party they're also bound to. What about the Lasombra that received orders from superiors on the clan to follow the defection?<br /> <br /> Oh, but they can't mingle with the dishonorable either, right? Well, the clan is defecting because it is in the clan's best interest and to save its colors, to avoid consumption by the Ancient in a stupid, ill thought war. Dishonor for an individual isn't the same as dishonor for a group or institution, and if you think it is, again it is your interpretation. If a follower does not see their own clan as dishonorable for making this decision, who are you to say otherwise?<br /> <br /> Especially if you consider, regardless of the V5 plot, the risks involved in a mass defection. A Honorable Lasombra could be tasked with guaranteeing safe escape for others in their area and be the last to follow behind, still defecting because the clan will need them if they live and the alternative is to become a traitor for real. I see no cowardice in following such an order, do not take the managerial decision as having the same moral weight of a personal decision.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat degenerated into treason or not? While it is true that they seem as united as ever, it is also true that they did so by ditching a lot of the goals and practices of the sect to embrace just a few, and by offing anyone who resisted the change. What does the Code of Milan has to say about it, if it is the bread and butter of Honorable Accord?<br /> <br /> Well, the Code has more than one version to begin with, and its creator is so pleased with the Sabbat adherence that he defected to the Camarilla at the end of the 90's, so at least him decided already the other sect is more honorable. The first two precepts talk about the Regent, the sect ditched the role of Regent entirely. Precept V commands to treat your peers fairly, not <i>fairly as long as they agree with your demented plan</i>. This is not about the follower not wanting the war, but witnessing those contrary to the war being hunted until they fled or died. Precept X calls for protecting territory, while the sect decided to leave the territory unprotected. Precept XI is <i>extremely</i> adamant on the importance of freedom, which definitely isn't how the sect currently conducts itself. Precept XIII demands support for the Black Hand, the sect ditched the Hand entirely as unnecessary (it could have been reformed instead to be cleansed of spies).<br /> <br /> And for those who follow the reformed Code from 1933, precept XVI demands action against any members that abuse their power and authority within the sect for personal gain at the expense of the sect as a whole. If a follower sees stomping on as many as 6 precepts, including those protecting the fundamental resources (territory) and goal (freedom) of the sect as abusing power at the sect's expense, they are bound by the Code to act against the leaders that did it.<br /> <br /> Yes, the most honorable course of action would be to take the fight and protect their vision of the Sabbat. But neither the Code or the Path demands stupidity. Victory from within isn't feasible, and for such a follower the sect as described in the Code is no more. The Camarilla isn't the enemy if there's no True Sabbat for them to oppose, and they're not dishonorable <i>per se</i>. The new &quot;Sabbat&quot; is. So if defection is the least bad option given the circumstances, and it protects your loyalty to your clan, why not?<br /> <br /> None of this must be agreed by all, most or even many Path followers. But to think everyone of them would disagree with this and follow an extremely narrow interpretation of their duties, the same interpretation everyone? <b>The very fact we're discussing this is proof that the Path can be interpreted otherwise</b>. To say that a single interpretation of it would hold water is to say that those disagreeing somehow do not understand the &quot;true meaning&quot; of the Path. This very discussion could exist within the setting with just a few adaptations among follower of Honorable Accord of high standing, either reflecting on those events or hypothesizing at them. So yes, Path followers can disagree on interpretation of their duties and still be followers of the same Path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475887#post1475887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I get that bit, my observation is that a path member is not only incredibly unlikely to defect but is also incredibly unlikely to even consider doing so. Nothing about the philosophy, sins or outlook even seems like it would even be considered outside of extreme personal situations.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my sincere opinion, yes, you are, sorry.<br /> <br /> They are still people, not computers. Quite capable people, by the way, if they achieved a reasonable ranking in the Path. And just as people they are perfectly capable of weighing exceptional actions on exceptional circumstances. Also of taking such actions even if in calmer nights they thought they never would, because saying you would never engage in something you abhor the notion is still easier when you're not in the grips of the actual circumstances that would call for it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> got it on spot. Paths aren't closed cultures, and they're not meant to have no room for failure, even against their greatest sins. A Path follower still exists in a broad world and have contact with other ideas. They're not a cult, because cults are meant to be closed systems, stripping members of as much contact with the outside world as possible, Path followers are meant to operate along other people as usual. And they're fully expected to have bad days and falls from grace. It isn't about absolute discipline, it is about staving off the Beast, a battle that is always ongoing with good days and bad days, victories and losses.<br /> <br /> A major loss isn't meant to be the end of the war against the Beast, no matter what that loss entails in the outside. And the rules are supportive of this, not of a tight interpretation where a particular sin stripes you of any hope of ever attaining higher ranks again or toss you directly into Wassail. Why would the Honorable Accord be the only Path that works this strictly? That's not in any way what the books say.<br /> <br /> Even <b>if</b> you assume the only reason for following <i>your entire clan</i> is personal fear. Not, I don't know, <i>loyalty to the clan.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T09:37:18-08:00","id":1475905,"title":"","content":"So It isn't the HA practitioners betraying the Sabbat, it's the Sabbat betraying everything they stand for (and the fans). <br /> <br /> It's too much ST fiat really. HA vampires are like, the most useful vampires to have around (so easy to manipulate) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T10:32:49-08:00","id":1475913,"title":"","content":"I think we've gotten a little off topic here. I think that there should be a substantial number of Road of Kings followers in the Camarilla. And there should be many Gangrel who follow the Road of the Beast, or the Path of the Feral Heart, who are nominally Camarilla or Anarch, but no notices because those Gangrel are wandering the interstates feeding on truckers and hitchhikers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T10:37:41-08:00","id":1475915,"title":"","content":"That depends on what you mean by substantial. Again, Humanity is too convenient a default for many Camarilla vampires going through the trouble of joining a Path, if they even know about it.<br /> <br /> But old followers and a few of their Childer? Sure thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T13:55:38-08:00","id":1475934,"title":"","content":"And, as has already been noted, that's been the case in the books for a long time (though most of the Cam-aligned if not joined Gangrel are on Harmony instead of Feral Heart as Beast off-shoots go).<br /> <br /> It's rare, but there have (even as a bit of a retcon) always been Path followers in the Cam. It's just a thing-we-don't-talk-about in the Cam for the most part to ensure the promotion of Humanity among the younger members.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T20:16:29-08:00","id":1475963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475034-paths-of-enlightenment-in-the-camarilla-v20?p=1475895#post1475895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as I understand it, the Sabbat basically said, &quot;Okay, all that talk about killing Antediluvians and stopped Gehenna? Well, it's go time! Time to fight or die, sink or swim.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Lasombra (and others but mostly the Lasombra) said, &quot;... naaaaah, I don't really want to die fighting the elders. Turns out this whole thing was just a LARP and we're gonna go join the Camarilla. Deuces!&quot;<br /> <br /> I have a hard time seeing vampires on the Path of Honorable Accord abandoning their faction, their allies and their very raison d'etre because they don't want to die. That mostly goes against all of the Path's precepts. Now at an individual level there would certainly be a few, but I imagine the vast majority of the Path followers would have been on the first red-eye flight to the Middle East to go fight. That would be my guess as to why there aren't any left - they all went to bravely face their Final Death.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you have a hard time seeing a Lasombra Path of Honorable Accord Follower being capable of feeling deeply torn between who to be loyal to, when they would be loyal to both sect and clan, and now suddenly both are making conflicting choices, that's kind of on you, and you holding following this path to a standard no other path of morality or even humanity has been, especially by the actual rules and material of the game. Following the path doesn't make you an automaton, no longer capable of nuanced thinking or decision making. And following the path doesn't preclude that sometimes now and then, like pretty much everyone else on every other path or humanity that isn't in Golconda, you fail at perfectly following it, especially when there are driving reasons pushing you to consider an act that would transgress it.<br /> <br /> Especially when, the problem in V5 plot shift is that the Sabbat has shifted in overall attitude, becoming far more brutal, feral, and especially to the point for someone on Honorable Accord, arbitrary, than their previous incarnation, to the point that it is noted that Honorable Accord followers end up repeatedly in conflict with something as simple as the Sabbat approaches to even mortal society due to their own philosophy. Honorable Accord demands a rigor of approach that would increasingly feel like it has no place in that Sabbat, (and in fact that is what results to the point of it being abandoned and pushed to the margins as a Forsaken Path, not the thing you are saying of &quot;well they all died&quot;). It feels reasonable just fine within the worldview and ethos of the Path for their to be room for a path follower to look at all that and decide they cannot abide by what they believe and remain in the Sabbat. Especially for a Lasombra path follower, who on top of seeing the very nature of his sect shift in that way, has to deal with that the leadership structure of their own clan that they answer to and have some loyalty to besides is going &quot;Marines we are leaving&quot;. Choosing to defect is entirely possible in these circumstances. But even a non Lasombra path follower is going to entirely, validly, start having second thoughts about the Sabbat in these circumstances. And some of these people might in fact act on those thoughts, because they aren't robots. And some of these people might not act on those thoughts, because they aren't robots. Path followers are not a monolith, especially in a V20 setup, the setup being discussed here to frame actions and choices in.<br /> <br /> And since the discussion here is that we're talking about V5 plot changes, with V20 setup, and what path followers would be doing in a setup like that, at that point the ones deciding to act/defect make a path check to see how much the choice hurts them on a spiritual level.<br /> <br /> And that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  Word choice fix. 03-07-2022, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}